{
  "name": "How to make a porch accessible for a wheelchair?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Making a porch accessible for a wheelchair involves a few key steps to ensure safety and usability. First, you'll need to accurately measure the rise from the ground level to your door's threshold. This measurement is critical because it dictates the length and slope of any ramp you might need. Next, check the available landing and turning space at both the top and bottom of your entry. A wheelchair user needs ample room to maneuver, especially when opening a door. Don't forget to review the door swing and how easily someone can reach the door hardware. You want everything to be within easy grasp. Finally, assess the site for potential constraints like drainage issues, how much snow and ice it might get, and where utilities are located. All these factors will influence the best design choice, whether it's a ramp, a lift, or even rebuilding the porch entirely. It’s important to select a solution that fits both the site and the user’s specific mobility needs, ensuring a stable, step-free, and safe entry.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
